5	 * order they were added, each keeping any figure a statement bound it to. Their name and aliases become aliases of the
6	 * other. Their patrons are added to the other's (not the other themselves, no repeats); anyone naming them as patron
7	 * names the other instead (not themselves, no repeats). Their pool memberships move to the other (shares added when the
8	 * other is already a member). The crews they lead are led by the other (who leaves those crews' members), and their crew
9	 * memberships move to the other (dropped where the other already leads or is in the crew). Their plans become the other's. Their statements become the other's, standing before the other's own, so the other's
10	 * last statement stays theirs (or, having none, becomes their last). Their holds, dated grades, watchers and contact
